00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:04.630 align:start position:0%
on march 21 2022 cd projekt red  announced the next game in the witcher  series has begun development which in  turn caused me to celebrate as if i had  just won the lottery it also brought up  a question i hadn't thought about in a  while what do i want from a witcher 3  follow-up so with elden rings still  burning on my mind i first started  writing this video with the plan of  telling you what i'd want the witcher to  take inspiration from however the  further i got into this script the more  i could hear my mind scream screw this  you're stripping all of the witcher out  so instead allow me to talk about what i  want from the next witcher game while  trying to not overdo the comparisons  so i've seen the reddit threads of  disapproval but i disagree i would love  to create my own witcher in the next  game initially i was on the fence about  this one but the more i thought about it  the more i realized that it's a change  that could work well for witcher i love  geralt but if the series is moving away  from him anyway then i'd love to step  into the boots of my own witcher and  play out my monster killing fantasy in  that way however i don't want it to be a  voiceless protagonist situation i'm  thinking more in the lines of mass  effect or cd projekt red's very own  cyberpunk 2077. each witcher would  already have a name baked into the  game's story as well as a plentiful  amount of voice dialogue choices for the  player to choose from cdpr could even  take an actual stab at real story  altering consequences to those choices  it's also worth noting that based on the  teaser this next entry will dive into  unknown territory with the school of the  links this school hasn't been explored  in any other piece of witcher media  aside from fan fiction there are also  theories that this could be a new school  that series started after witcher 3  marrying the styles of the wolf school  and the cat school but if siri isn't the  star of this next game and the lead is  an unknown witcher then why not let me  customize them  as i'm making this video there are  probably a dozen people crafting tweets  about how amazing eldon rings organic  discovery is the witcher 3 is also a  game guilty of being a joy to explore  but as i returned to the northern realms  recently i found it a little less  organic with witcher's map you're drawn  to most locations because of a looming  question mark taunting you it drives  your curiosity forward and what you find  may lead to a cool experience but it's  less of a surprise because you already  knew something was there and sure you  can filter these off of the map but it's  not permanent and they populate the  second you open the map again you can  reconfigure the hud and take  undiscovered locations off of the  mini-map or axe the hud entirely but in  the next witcher i'd like the option to  truly have an empty map to reference i'd  also love for there to be a compass at  the top of the screen so that when i do  take off the mini-map i still have a  minimal way to keep track of where i'm  headed ultimately i want the next  witcher to have some mystery but just  not as much mystery as elvenring has  what i mean by that is the witcher needs  its cutscenes it needs its main story  beats told or shown directly to the  player in a classic game way and i know  eldon ring has its cutscenes too but  it's story is mainly told through item  descriptions and context clues from  small moments of npc dialogue and that's  definitely not something i want from  witcher instead that mystery can show up  more inside content in the  moment-to-moment gameplay of getting  from point a to point b the world of the  witcher is so vast and detailed and i  think there are a ton of opportunities  for the devs to bake nuggets of intrigue  into the corners of the game there's no  denying it the witcher 3's map is big  and it does a great job of giving the  player the feeling of being in a living  breathing world however i'd love to  stand on a shore and see skelega in the  distance and sail to it instead of  sitting through a loading screen in the  next witcher i love more connectivity  with the maps different regions if  there's a palace like the one in vezima  let me travel to the city and gaze in  awe as i ride up to the palace gates let  me journey back and forth freely to this  game's version of karamorin without  loading straight into it this is a small  issue and if we're really being honest  the loads won't even matter on the ssds  of current consoles but at this point  i'm used to everything being connected  in open world games that i can't help  but expect it from the witcher as well  hopefully this doesn't seem hypocritical  to my last point but i would love a  quicker fast travel system in witcher 3  if i'm out in a field and want to get to  a town across the map i have to first  travel to the nearest signpost in order  to warp to another signpost this is slow  and unnecessary i want the next witcher  to be more like modern open worlds and  allow me to jump straight to where i  want to go without extra steps and  please don't make me use resources to  fast travel that's right i'm looking at  you horizon  it bears repeating that the world of the  witcher is large but so far in the games  we've only gotten the chance to explore  one chunk of it so in the next game i'd  love to take a trip south of the  northern kingdoms i want to know what  it's like to explore nilfgaard even  though word on the street is they suck  over there let me get lost in more  swamps and forests let me climb the  mountains and drool at the vistas that  await me let me travel to the desert and  regret it take me to wherever the school  of the lynx is and let me fall in love  with the areas that surround it  this may be hard to hear but the witcher  3's crafting system needs to calm down  resources may be everywhere you go but  the list of required ingredients per  item can still get a little overwhelming  so for the next witcher game i'd love a  simplified crafting system and a more  streamlined way of upgrading my favorite  gear shout out to the homies marcus and  nick louise for helping me brainstorm  that one and while we're talking about  crafting in gear it'd be really cool to  get a transmog system going in the new  witcher game as well that way i can have  the stats of an awesome piece of armor  but change the appearance to better  match my entire outfit  as much as i love witcher 3 i was never  crazy about how geralt handled when just  walking around the addition of the  alternate movement option definitely  made this better but it still hasn't  aids super well however i'm assuming  this will be a pretty easy fix  considering the next game will be in  unreal 5 a completely different engine  than the witcher 3 was developed in this  shift in engine should also change how  the combat feels which would also be a  welcome change the witcher 3 combat  isn't bad in my opinion but it doesn't  feel as good as it once did  my next request has nothing to do with  gameplay changes i really want honesty  and transparency from cd projekt red the  studio was riding high after the release  of witcher 3 and many fans myself  included felt that they could do no  wrong that bubble was popped when the  broken cyberpunk 2077 experience got  into player hands now the company is in  a state of repairing its image and  restoring trust with fans following the  announcement of the next witcher i saw a  mix of excitement and caution with many  fans restricting themselves for getting  too hyped about the next witcher release  even another close friend of mine and  fellow witcher enthusiasts reacted to  the news of the next game in the text  thread and said quote nice to hear but  after cyberpunk i'll have to wait on it  for me personally i was never super  excited about cyberpunk i planned on  playing it but i wasn't in the camp of  fans that thought it would be the next  evolution of rpg so when it released i  calmly decided to hold off on playing it  i wasn't let down by the train wreck  like many others were however i know for  a fact if that same situation happens  with the next witcher game  i  will be devastated so i'd love more than  anything for cdpr to learn from their  past mistakes and be honest with fans  about the progress of the project and if  it's not done then delay it into  infinity just please don't ship a broken  game or rush it to make a deadline or  sync up with the next netflix witcher  release  okay my last request is one that i'm  super unsure about but hang in there  with me i love the message system in  eldon ring and if i'm being completely  honest with myself i'd love something  similar in a witcher game however i  don't feel like it meshes with witcher  lore well and we also don't need a  kikimura encounter preceded by a dog  ahead try gesture message this seems  more like a feature for a witcher mmo  something else i'd be mildly interested  in  so to recap i want a character creator  more organic exploration with a compass  and seamlessly connected regions from  witcher lore that we've never explored  before better fast travel better  movement and developer transparency so  did i nail it or did i nail it hit the  comment section and let me know what you  really want from the next witcher game  and make sure you're subscribed to  gamespot so that when more information  about the game comes out you can stay  informed thanks for watching  [Music]
 

